From e0f26c6c14732d1a5089338a6cd0fb82e06178fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Gurov <aliogu23@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 04:27:44 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Launcher3: Add Visual effects toggles for blur and window
 corners

Blur behind the app drawer and recents, and the legacy blur behind
apps, cost noticeable frame time on high-refresh panels. On dizi
(Adreno 710, 2560x1600@120) an app drawer fling is 6.64% janky (p90
18 ms) with drawer blur versus 2.25-2.30% (p90 7 ms) without, and
icon to app launch drops from 3.2-3.5% to 0.66% janky with the behind
apps blur off. The upstream flags are READ_ONLY aconfig flags, so they
cannot be changed at runtime.

Add VisualEffects, which reads the user's choices once per process
from the launcher shared preferences. allAppsBlur() and
enableOverviewBackgroundWallpaperBlur() return the flag value and the
user choice, so turning a toggle off takes the flag-off code path, and
every call site is routed through it. BaseDepthController gates depth
blur per state: app drawer, overview, and everything else, which is
treated as behind apps. The scaling workspace reveal and the back
animation honour the behind apps toggle. WindowCorners wraps the
QuickStepContract corner radius for window animations so rounded
corners can be disabled too; measurements show no gain from that, so
it stays on by default.

Add a Settings > Visual effects screen with four switches: blur
behind app drawer, blur behind recents and blur while opening apps
(all default off), and rounded corners in animations (default on).
The values are cached per process, so SettingsActivity restarts the
launcher when leaving settings after a change.

